  <name>Bluet</name>
  <summary>Manage Bluetooth devices and connections</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.suryavamsi6">
    <name>Surya Vamsi</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Bluet is a native Bluetooth manager drawn directly on the GPU with GPUI,
      without a browser or Electron. It talks to the system BlueZ service, so
      what you see is the real state of your adapters and devices.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Turn adapters on and off and control their visibility</li>
      <li>Discover, pair, connect, trust and forget devices</li>
      <li>Answer PIN, passkey and confirmation requests in the app</li>
      <li>See battery levels reported by connected devices</li>
      <li>Change volume, mute and audio profiles of Bluetooth audio devices</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Bluet needs a running BlueZ service and a Vulkan-capable graphics driver.
      Audio controls use the PulseAudio or PipeWire server of your session.
    </p>
  </description>
